  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "94d124ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Raw per-frame gaze distribution, anchored vs. non-anchored trials\n",
    "\n",
    "Every individual eye-camera frame (not trial-averaged), assigned to its\n",
    "trial's population anchoring state, plotted in raw pixel space -- checking\n",
    "whether the 2D cloud of gaze positions actually shifts to a different\n",
    "location/spread when the population is non-anchored, rather than just being\n",
    "noisier by the same summary metric."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "94949e83",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-31T08:45:02.771502Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-31T08:45:02.771319Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-31T08:45:03.973955Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-31T08:45:03.973617Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 450x450 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "anchored frames: mean=(121.8, 95.9), std=(1.3, 0.8)\n",
      "non-anchored frames: mean=(121.8, 96.0), std=(1.5, 0.9)\n",
      "Mann-Whitney anchored vs non-anchored: eye_x p=0.0437, eye_y p=1.76e-24\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "Assign each individual eye-camera frame to its trial (via nearest-sample\n",
    "lookup against the Blender-derived trial_number channel, which lives on a\n",
    "different clock/sample-rate than the eye camera -- pynapple's `value_from`\n",
    "keeps the CALLER's timestamps and pulls in the nearest VALUE from its\n",
    "argument, so `eye_x.value_from(trial_number)` is the right direction here),\n",
    "then to that trial's population anchored/non-anchored state, and plot the\n",
    "raw 2D pixel distribution split by state. Blink/tracking-loss frames (same\n",
    "mask as the position-binned analysis above) are dropped so the comparison\n",
    "isn't dominated by rare near-zero-coordinate artifact frames.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "eye_x_mat = nap.Tsd(t=np.array(beh['eye_x'].index), d=np.array(beh['eye_x'].values))\n",
    "trial_num_per_eye_frame = np.array(eye_x_mat.value_from(beh['trial_number']).values)\n",
    "eye_x_raw = np.array(beh['eye_x'].values)\n",
    "eye_y_raw = np.array(beh['eye_y'].values)\n",
    "\n",
    "first_trial = int(tns[0])\n",
    "trial_idx_per_frame = np.round(trial_num_per_eye_frame).astype(int) - first_trial   # 0-indexed, matches frac_anchored\n",
    "in_range = (trial_idx_per_frame >= 0) & (trial_idx_per_frame < n_trials) & (~blink_mask)\n",
    "\n",
    "frame_frac_anchored = np.full(len(trial_idx_per_frame), np.nan)\n",
    "frame_frac_anchored[in_range] = frac_anchored[trial_idx_per_frame[in_range]]\n",
    "\n",
    "anchored_frames = in_range & (frame_frac_anchored > 0.5)\n",
    "nonanchored_frames = in_range & (frame_frac_anchored <= 0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.5, 4.5))\n",
    "ax.scatter(eye_x_raw[nonanchored_frames], eye_y_raw[nonanchored_frames], s=1, alpha=0.15,\n",
    "           color=NONANCH_COLOR, label=f'non-anchored (n={nonanchored_frames.sum()} frames)')\n",
    "ax.scatter(eye_x_raw[anchored_frames], eye_y_raw[anchored_frames], s=1, alpha=0.15,\n",
    "           color=ANCH_COLOR, label=f'anchored (n={anchored_frames.sum()} frames)')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('eye_x (px)')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('eye_y (px)')\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'M{MOUSE}D{DAY}: raw pupil centroid, per frame', fontsize=9)\n",
    "leg = ax.legend(fontsize=7, markerscale=8)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(os.path.join(FIGPATH, f'eye_position_raw_scatter_M{MOUSE}D{DAY}.pdf'), dpi=200, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'anchored frames: mean=({np.nanmean(eye_x_raw[anchored_frames]):.1f}, {np.nanmean(eye_y_raw[anchored_frames]):.1f}), '\n",
    "      f'std=({np.nanstd(eye_x_raw[anchored_frames]):.1f}, {np.nanstd(eye_y_raw[anchored_frames]):.1f})')\n",
    "print(f'non-anchored frames: mean=({np.nanmean(eye_x_raw[nonanchored_frames]):.1f}, {np.nanmean(eye_y_raw[nonanchored_frames]):.1f}), '\n",
    "      f'std=({np.nanstd(eye_x_raw[nonanchored_frames]):.1f}, {np.nanstd(eye_y_raw[nonanchored_frames]):.1f})')\n",
    "\n",
    "u_x, p_x = mannwhitneyu(eye_x_raw[anchored_frames], eye_x_raw[nonanchored_frames], alternative='two-sided')\n",
    "u_y, p_y = mannwhitneyu(eye_y_raw[anchored_frames], eye_y_raw[nonanchored_frames], alternative='two-sided')\n",
    "print(f'Mann-Whitney anchored vs non-anchored: eye_x p={p_x:.3g}, eye_y p={p_y:.3g}')\n"
   ]
  },
