   "source": [
    "## Pupil size (dilation) vs. population anchoring state\n",
    "\n",
    "Pupil diameter is a common physiological proxy for arousal/attentional\n",
    "state, independent of *where* the eye is pointed. Checked here the same way\n",
    "as gaze position above: trial-level (position-binned, blink- and\n",
    "zero-fill-corrected `eye_dil_trials` from the setup cell), a trial-ordered\n",
    "raster alongside the population anchoring strip, and the raw per-frame\n",
    "distribution (reusing the exact `anchored_frames`/`nonanchored_frames` masks\n",
    "from the gaze analysis, so it's directly comparable)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
